---
import PlaceholderBadge from '../components/PlaceholderBadge.astro';
import SocialLinks from '../components/SocialLinks.astro';
import { LINKS, SITE } from '../consts';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// TODO: confirm order, years and titles. Listed newest first.
const timeline = [
	{
		org: 'GIC',
		period: '20XX – now',
		role: 'Software Engineer',
		note: 'Investment platforms for a sovereign wealth fund',
	},
	{
		org: 'WSO2',
		period: '20XX – 20XX',
		role: 'Software Engineer',
		note: 'Integration and API infrastructure',
	},
	{
		org: 'DirectFN',
		period: '20XX – 20XX',
		role: 'Software Engineer',
		note: 'Trading and market data platforms for regional exchanges and brokers',
	},
];
---

<Layout title="About" description={`How I spent ${SITE.yearsInIndustry} years building capital markets technology.`}>
	<div class="container-page pt-14">
		<p class="label">/about</p>
		<div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
			<h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg">About</h1>
			<PlaceholderBadge />
		</div>

		<div class="mt-10 grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_18rem]">
			<!-- TODO: rewrite in your own voice. Keep it a story, not a CV. -->
			<div class="prose">
				<p class="text-xl leading-relaxed">
					I've spent the last {SITE.yearsInIndustry} years building software where a wrong number costs real money
					and a slow one costs a trade.
				</p>

				<h2>DirectFN: learning where the latency hides</h2>
				<p>
					I started at DirectFN, building trading and market data platforms used by brokers and exchanges across
					the Middle East and South Asia. It was the best possible introduction to the domain: order types,
					market sessions, corporate actions, and the difference between a system that works and one that works
					at the open. I learned to read a flame graph before I learned to write a design doc.
				</p>

				<h2>WSO2: thinking in platforms</h2>
				<p>
					At WSO2 I moved one layer down, to integration and API infrastructure that other teams build on. The
					lesson was about contracts: versioning, backward compatibility, and designing so the next engineer, who
					you'll never meet, can't easily misuse your API. It changed how I write code for everyone after.
				</p>

				<h2>GIC: correctness at scale</h2>
				<p>
					At GIC I work on platforms that support investment decisions for a sovereign wealth fund. The problems
					are less about microseconds and more about correctness under failure: idempotent processing,
					reconciliation, auditability, and systems that are calm to operate at 3am. This is where most of the
					ideas in my <a href="/blog">blog series</a> come from.
				</p>

				<h2>What I care about</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Boring, explicit designs.</strong> A single writer beats a clever lock.</li>
					<li><strong>Failure as a first-class path.</strong> Retries, replays and duplicates are normal, not edge cases.</li>
					<li><strong>Writing things down.</strong> Design notes outlive the code and the people who wrote it.</li>
				</ul>

				<p>
					Outside work: TODO, a line or two about you as a person (it's what people remember from an about
					page).
				</p>
			</div>

			<aside class="space-y-6">
				<div class="panel">
					<div class="panel-head">experience</div>
					<ol class="relative p-4">
						{
							timeline.map((t, i) => (
								<li class="relative border-l border-line pb-6 pl-5 last:pb-0">
									<span
										class:list={[
											'absolute top-1.5 -left-[4.5px] h-2 w-2 rounded-full',
											i === 0 ? 'bg-accent' : 'bg-line',
										]}
										aria-hidden="true"
									/>
									<p class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-fg">{t.org}</p>
									<p class="font-mono text-xs text-faint tabular">{t.period}</p>
									<p class="mt-1 text-sm text-fg">{t.role}</p>
									<p class="text-sm text-muted">{t.note}</p>
								</li>
							))
						}
					</ol>
				</div>
				<div class="panel p-4">
					<p class="text-sm text-muted">Want the full version?</p>
					<a href={LINKS.resume} class="btn btn-primary mt-3">résumé.pdf <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
					<SocialLinks class="mt-4" />
				</div>
			</aside>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>
